    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i'm working on a documentary script about the mau mau uprising in kenya. can u give me a timeline of the main events but really focus on the perspective of the kenyan fighters and the people living under colonial rule? i want to capture their struggle against the british administration.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The historical record offers a fragmented and often suppressed perspective on the Mau Mau uprising, leaving historians to reconstruct the experience of Kenyan ancestors through partial accounts, folklore, and the traumatic legacy of trauma and displacement. The uprising, which lasted from roughly 1952 to 1960, was a desperate resistance by the Kikuyua and other Kaluku communities against forced assimilation into British colonial structures. Your documentary could vividly contrast the grim realities of concentration camps, the forced labor, and the brutal suppression tactics used by colonial forces with the fierce, communal spirit of the fighters who organized to protect their land and dignity. Ultimately, honoring their struggle requires centering their voices and emotional journeys to reveal the human cost of resistance that official histories often erased.",
